# Core rules

> Full system prompt: `CLAUDE.md`. This file is the rules section, slimmed for Cursor's context budget. The two are kept in sync.

## Stack
Expo SDK 55 · RN 0.83 · React 19 · TS 5.9 strict · Zustand · TanStack Query · axios · RHF + Zod · NativeWind v4 · FlashList · expo-image · MMKV + expo-secure-store · Sentry · PostHog · Biome · pnpm.

## Process
- Run `pnpm before-pr` before considering code complete.
- Commit format: Conventional Commits — `type(scope): description`.
- One opinionated way per concern.

## Architecture
- Server state via TanStack Query; UI state via Zustand. Never duplicate.
- Auth tokens only via `expo-secure-store` (`@/lib/secureStorage`). Non-secret prefs → MMKV. Never the reverse.
- All HTTP via `@/lib/api` (centralized axios). Biome blocks direct `axios`/`fetch` imports.
- Validate every external response with Zod (use `getValidated`).
- Forms: RHF + Zod resolver. One schema per form. Export schema for tests.

## Naming
- Screens: `PascalCase` + `Screen` suffix → `app/screens/profile/ProfileScreen.tsx`.
- Navigators: `PascalCase` + `Navigator` suffix.
- Hooks: `useCamelCase.ts`.
- Zustand: `useNameStore.ts`.
- Query hooks: `useResourceVerb.ts`.
- Components: `PascalCase.tsx`. Tests co-located.
- Screens grouped by feature subdirectory, never flat in `screens/`.

## Components
- Use custom primitives from `@/components` — never raw `react-native` `Text`/`Button`/`TextInput`/`FlatList`/`Image`/`SafeAreaView`. Biome enforces.
- Lists with >30 items: `ListView` (FlashList) with required `estimatedItemSize`.
- Images: `@/components/Image` (wraps `expo-image`). Always pass a `placeholder` for network images.

## Styling
- Tokens live in `tailwind.config.js` only. No hex, no literal spacing/radius/font-size anywhere else.
- Variants via `tailwind-variants` (`tv()`).
- Dark mode via `dark:` prefix.
- RTL via `me-*`/`ms-*` margin utilities.
- No inline `style={{ … }}` for visual values.

## i18n + a11y
- Every user-visible string via `translate(key)` or `tx` prop. Hardcoded English → reject.
- Every Pressable: `accessibilityRole` + `accessibilityLabel`.
- Respect `useReduceMotion`. Hit-slop ≥ 8 on small targets.
- Live regions on async status changes.

## Errors + logging
- `api` returns normalized errors. Surface to UI via banners/`ErrorState`.
- Sentry capture only at error boundaries / explicit catches.
- No `console.log` in production paths — use `@/lib/logger`.

## Performance
- Memoize list renderers (`React.memo` + `useCallback`).
- `FlashList` `estimatedItemSize` is required.
- Reanimated worklets only on UI thread.

## Privacy + security
- Declare data collection in `PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy`.
- PostHog `identify` only after consent.
- No PII in logs.
- Env access only via `@/config/env`.
- Never commit `.env*` or secrets.

## Tests
- Mock at the network boundary only (MSW). Never mock our own modules.
- Render with the same providers the app uses (helper).
- One user-flow test per screen minimum.
- Don't snapshot components > 30 lines.

## UI states
- Every screen handles loading, empty, error, populated. Use `LoadingState`/`EmptyState`/`ErrorState` primitives.
